content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Business Owner",
      "description": "Person responsible for submitting records and approving financial actions."
    },
    {
      "name": "Monthly Sales Document",
      "description": "Report showing sales activity for a given month."
    },
    {
      "name": "Expense",
      "description": "Cost incurred by the business that must be recorded."
    },
    {
      "name": "Accountant",
      "description": "Professional who prepares entries, reviews data, and manages invoices."
    },
    {
      "name": "Account",
      "description": "Financial record containing entries, owner details, and receipts.",
      "attributes": [
        "Financial Entry",
        "Business Owner",
        "Receipt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Financial Entry",
      "description": "Recorded financial transaction created from business documents."
    },
    {
      "name": "Receipt",
      "description": "Proof of purchase used to validate expenses."
    },
    {
      "name": "Invoice",
      "description": "Billing document issued to a client for services or products."
    },
    {
      "name": "Client",
      "description": "Customer who receives invoices and pays the business."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bookkeeper",
      "description": "Person who records expenses and organizes receipts."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inconsistency Notification",
      "description": "Message alerting the accountant about missing or conflicting data."
    },
    {
      "name": "Auditor",
      "description": "Independent reviewer ensuring financial statements meet regulations."
    },
    {
      "name": "Financial Statement",
      "description": "Formal report summarizing the business’s financial performance."
    },
    {
      "name": "Regulations",
      "description": "Financial rules and standards the business must follow."
    },
    {
      "name": "Document Request",
      "description": "Request from the auditor to obtain additional documentation."
    },
    {
      "name": "Supporting Document",
      "description": "Additional evidence provided to verify financial transactions."
    },
    {
      "name": "Finance Review",
      "description": "Final assessment confirming compliance with financial rules."
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Accounting": {
      "objects": [
        "Business Owner",
        "Accountant",
        "Monthly Sales Document",
        "Account",
        "Financial Entry"
      ]
    },
    "Auditing": {
      "objects": [
        "Auditor",
        "Financial Statement",
        "Document Request",
        "Supporting Document",
        "Finance Review"
      ]
    },
    "Billing": {
      "objects": [
        "Invoice",
        "Client",
        "Business Owner"
      ]
    },
    "Bookkeeping": {
      "objects": [
        "Bookkeeper",
        "Expense",
        "Inconsistency Notification",
        "Receipt"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Accounting": {
      "derived from": "Accounting Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Accounting Customer",
        "Accountant",
        "Monthly Sales Document",
        "Account",
        "Financial Entry"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Business Owner -> Accounting Customer"
      ]
    },
    "Auditing": {
      "derived from": "Auditing Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Auditor",
        "Financial Statement",
        "Document Request",
        "Supporting Document",
        "Finance Review"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Billing": {
      "derived from": "Billing Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Invoice",
        "Customer Client",
        "Business Owner"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Client -> Customer Client"
      ]
    },
    "Bookkeeping": {
      "derived from": "Bookkeeping Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Bookkeeper",
        "Expense",
        "Inconsistency Notification",
        "Receipt"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
